.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt DSA_SIZE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm DSA_size ,
.Nm DSA_bits ,
.Nm DSA_security_bits
.Nd get DSA signature size, key bits or security bits
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/dsa.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft int
.Fo DSA_bits
.Fa "const DSA *dsa"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DSA_size
.Fa "const DSA *dsa"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DSA_security_bits
.Fa "const DSA *dsa"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_bits 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_security_bits 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_size 3 .
.Pp
.Fn DSA_bits
returns the number of bits in key
.Fa dsa :
this is the number of bits in the
.Em p
parameter.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_size
returns the maximum size of an ASN.1 encoded DSA signature for key
.Fa dsa
in bytes.
It can be used to determine how much memory must be allocated for a DSA
signature.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_security_bits
returns the number of security bits of the given
.Fa dsa
key.
See
.Xr BN_security_bits 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn DSA_security_bits
returns the number of security bits in the key, or -1 if
.Fa dsa
doesn't hold any key parameters.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_bits
returns the number of bits in the key, or -1 if
.Fa dsa
doesn't hold any key parameters.
.Pp
.Fn DSA_size
returns the signature size in bytes, or -1 if
.Fa dsa
doesn't hold any key parameters.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_bits 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_security_bits 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_size 3 ,
.Xr DSA_new 3 ,
.Xr DSA_sign 3
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
